  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "41161522",
      "title": "Outputting Dynamic Values",
      "lectureOrder": 18,
      "videoOrder": 16,
      "sourceHash": "5b514a88487dd84abfc78a63ed6b607be66311ea7233c82e22f56dc82eb89308",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.231,
          "end": 4.47,
          "en": "So we got our first custom component here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.47,
          "end": 8.04,
          "en": "and it won't be the last component we'll work on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.04,
          "end": 8.873,
          "en": "At the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.873,
          "end": 10.77,
          "en": "it doesn't have any fancy styling,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.77,
          "end": 12.45,
          "en": "but we'll add some styling soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.45,
          "end": 15.42,
          "en": "But I'd like to make it a bit more dynamic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.42,
          "end": 19.47,
          "en": "And for that, I'll start by going to Post.jsx.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.47,
          "end": 22.44,
          "en": "And then there, outside of the component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.44,
          "end": 24.27,
          "en": "though it doesn't really matter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.27,
          "end": 27.18,
          "en": "I'll add a new constant called names,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.18,
          "end": 30.33,
          "en": "which holds an array of two possible names,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.33,
          "end": 33.207,
          "en": "Maximilian and Manuel.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.207,
          "end": 35.49,
          "en": "And I wanna output one of the two names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.49,
          "end": 37.86,
          "en": "whenever this component is rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 37.86,
          "end": 40.29,
          "en": "So basically, whenever I reload the page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.29,
          "end": 44.46,
          "en": "and I therefore cause React to re-render the screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.46,
          "end": 47.82,
          "en": "I wanna make sure that React picks one of the two names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.82,
          "end": 49.89,
          "en": "and outputs it on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.89,
          "end": 51.87,
          "en": "So that it's not always Maximilian,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 51.87,
          "end": 55.173,
          "en": "but we get some randomness on this website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.25,
          "end": 57.903,
          "en": "Now, how could we make this work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 58.8,
          "end": 60.63,
          "en": "Well, in order to make this work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 60.63,
          "end": 63.06,
          "en": "we first of all must add some logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 63.06,
          "end": 66.87,
          "en": "to this component function to pick a random name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 66.87,
          "end": 69.633,
          "en": "So we could add a constant called chosenName.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 71.07,
          "end": 74.52,
          "en": "And then here, I wanna call Math.random,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 74.52,
          "end": 76.8,
          "en": "this built-in random method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 76.8,
          "end": 79.59,
          "en": "that's supported by browsers out of the way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 79.59,
          "end": 82.28999999999999,
          "en": "So this is absolutely not React code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 82.28999999999999,
          "end": 84.093,
          "en": "this is all built-in instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 84.93,
          "end": 89.93,
          "en": "And, if what I get here is greater than 0.5,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 89.94,
          "end": 92.19,
          "en": "I wanna pick the first name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 92.19,
          "end": 96.513,
          "en": "So names zero, otherwise names one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.58,
          "end": 100.47,
          "en": "So with that, I have a 50-50 chance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.47,
          "end": 103.44,
          "en": "of picking Maximilian or Manuel.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 103.44,
          "end": 107.64,
          "en": "Now this, as mentioned here, is standard JavaScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 107.64,
          "end": 109.8,
          "en": "And it's important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 109.8,
          "end": 112.08,
          "en": "that even though this will be treated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 112.08,
          "end": 114.99000000000001,
          "en": "as a component by React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 114.99000000000001,
          "end": 116.7,
          "en": "it, in the end, still is a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 116.7,
          "end": 119.46000000000001,
          "en": "that will be executed by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 119.46000000000001,
          "end": 121.8,
          "en": "And therefore, in this component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 121.8,
          "end": 125.25,
          "en": "you can in the end run any JavaScript code you want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 125.25,
          "end": 126.663,
          "en": "in that function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 127.53,
          "end": 129.87,
          "en": "It's just important that in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 129.87,
          "end": 133.113,
          "en": "your function returns some JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 134.61,
          "end": 136.47,
          "en": "So here, I'm picking a random name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 136.47,
          "end": 138.63,
          "en": "And I now wanna output that name here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 138.63,
          "end": 141.54,
          "en": "instead of always outputting Maximilian.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 141.54,
          "end": 145.743,
          "en": "But, how do we get this chosenName from here to here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 146.91,
          "end": 149.91,
          "en": "Well, for that, we'll use a special syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 149.91,
          "end": 153.32999999999998,
          "en": "that's supported by JSX and React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 153.32999999999998,
          "end": 155.88,
          "en": "Instead of hard-coding the value here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 155.88,
          "end": 157.5,
          "en": "between these paragraph tags,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 157.5,
          "end": 160.68,
          "en": "as we're currently doing it with Maximilian,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 160.68,
          "end": 163.92000000000002,
          "en": "we add opening and closing curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 163.92000000000002,
          "end": 168.66,
          "en": "Single opening and single closing curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 168.66,
          "end": 171.81,
          "en": "And between those curly braces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 171.81,
          "end": 175.5,
          "en": "you can put any JavaScript expression of your choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 175.5,
          "end": 177.603,
          "en": "Like, for example, two plus two.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 178.77,
          "end": 182.1,
          "en": "If you do that and you save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 182.1,
          "end": 185.523,
          "en": "you'll see that now we get four as a output here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 186.6,
          "end": 189.3,
          "en": "We get four here because when you use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 189.3,
          "end": 193.83,
          "en": "this special curly brace syntax in your JSX code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 193.83,
          "end": 197.07,
          "en": "React will go ahead and take whatever is written",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 197.07,
          "end": 201.36,
          "en": "inside of those curly braces and execute it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 201.36,
          "end": 203.22,
          "en": "and then output the result",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 203.22,
          "end": 206.16,
          "en": "of that expression that was executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 206.16,
          "end": 207.81,
          "en": "So in this case, we have two plus two",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 207.81,
          "end": 211.263,
          "en": "hence the result four is output on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 212.46,
          "end": 214.29,
          "en": "And we can, of course, not just perform",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 214.29,
          "end": 216.45,
          "en": "mathematical calculations here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 216.45,
          "end": 221.07,
          "en": "but, instead, we can also reference variables or constants.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 221.07,
          "end": 224.01,
          "en": "So here I can output chosenName.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 224.01,
          "end": 227.43,
          "en": "And instead of outputting the text chosenName now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 227.43,
          "end": 230.94,
          "en": "as it would do without the curly braces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 230.94,
          "end": 233.934,
          "en": "here we get the text, chosenName,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 233.934,
          "end": 236.46,
          "en": "with those curly braces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 236.46,
          "end": 239.88,
          "en": "it will instead look into that constant or variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 239.88,
          "end": 243.39,
          "en": "and output the value that's stored in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 243.39,
          "end": 246.843,
          "en": "So now, we'll get either Maximilian or Manuel.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 247.83,
          "end": 249.69,
          "en": "Right now, it's Maximilian for me here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 249.69,
          "end": 251.31,
          "en": "but as I reload this page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 251.31,
          "end": 255.423,
          "en": "you see that it switches between these two names here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 256.29,
          "end": 258.63,
          "en": "And it switches after every reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 258.63,
          "end": 263.22,
          "en": "because a reload technically restarts the React application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 263.22,
          "end": 265.32,
          "en": "and causes all React components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 265.32,
          "end": 267.99,
          "en": "to be re-rendered on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 267.99,
          "end": 270.54,
          "en": "And even though this randomness is not a feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 270.54,
          "end": 272.76,
          "en": "we'll need in the finished application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 272.76,
          "end": 275.13,
          "en": "it is super important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 275.13,
          "end": 277.56,
          "en": "how you can output dynamic values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 277.56,
          "end": 280.02,
          "en": "in your React applications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 280.02,
          "end": 281.52,
          "en": "Because even though you might not need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 281.52,
          "end": 283.74,
          "en": "random values too often,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 283.74,
          "end": 287.58,
          "en": "you do very often need the results of calculations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 287.58,
          "end": 291.03,
          "en": "of data fetched from some backend API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 291.03,
          "end": 294.36,
          "en": "Something we'll also do later in this course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 294.36,
          "end": 298.02,
          "en": "are all kinds of other dynamic values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 298.02,
          "end": 300.3,
          "en": "So this is an important piece of syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 300.3,
          "end": 301.713,
          "en": "you must keep in mind.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
